# Vehicle / driver document readers ignore superseded copies (nihas V1.0.58).
# get_compliance_summary, get_expiring_documents, compute_compliance_score and
# is_compliance_blocking skip a live row when a newer live row of the same slot
# (org, entity, doc_type) has a different expiry — the same rule as
# features/compliance/utils/currentDocument.util.ts. Adds
# private.entity_document_is_superseded (closed to anon/authenticated).
# Function bodies start from the live prod definitions (adr010 20270915103200 for
# summary/expiring; 20260828010000 for score/blocking). No data, table or policy change.
#
# Not in this set:
#   supabase/release-manual/20261120055411_entity_documents_superseded_readers.rollback.sql
#     (manual rollback only, owner-run if the migration must be undone)
#   scripts/entity-documents-dedupe/ (read-only report; generated apply.sql is a
#     separate data change that needs review and the owner's GO)
#
# This version sorts before the repo's 2027-dated migrations; db-push-set uses
# --include-all on a snapshot, so the order is handled there.
#
# Apply only via: npm run db:push-set -- entity-documents-superseded-readers   (dry-run first; prod apply needs Vasanth's GO)
# Never via plain `supabase db push` / `npm run db:push`.
#
# Verify before applying:
#   npx jest supabase/migrations/__tests__/entityDocumentsSupersededReadersReleaseSet.test.ts
